        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "An employee may use up to a maximum of fifteen (15) paid days per calendar year for the purpose of arranging for the care of him/her self or his/her child(ren) or for attending to necessary legal proceedings or activities in instances where the employee or his/her child(ren) is a victim of domestic abuse and where the employee is not the perpetrator. Said fifteen (15) paid days are in addition to any other paid leave which the employee may accrue under the provisions of this agreement.",
